TASK-288 runtime harness: OpenSearch discovery in the running app and the
Settings > Search marker. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply,
build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task288-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # a loopback site on 127.0.0.1:8288 whose / links /opensearch.xml
    # (template http://127.0.0.1:8288/search?q={searchTerms}):
    python3 -m http.server 8288 --bind 127.0.0.1   # in the fixture directory
    OUT=<dir>; DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify288 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # "SHOOT <windowNumber> settings": `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber>`;
    # wait for "done" (about 20 s), kill that pid, then:
    git apply -R docs/harness/task288-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Loads http://127.0.0.1:8288/ in a new normal tab, then a second page of the
site, then http://localhost:8288/ in a Private window, logging the store
after each; then opens Settings > Search for a capture.

Results (2026-11-07): "Fixture Docs" added after the first load, no keyword,
isDiscovered, template http://127.0.0.1:8288/search?q=%s; the server saw
/opensearch.xml once (not for the second page); the Private page loaded and
nothing was fetched or added. A second launch on the same data dir kept the
entry and fetched no description (the site is listed). Settings showed the
row with "From site" in the Keyword column (the first label, "Added from
site", truncated in the 100 pt column).

